/ cancel %task% stops it: the goal never gets past its sleep, so it never answers "went on" — a wait on it fails as
/ Cancelled.
Start
- goal.call(Name="Slow", Parallel=true); variable.set(Name=%task%, Value=%!data%)
- task.cancel(Task=%task%)
- task.wait(Task=%task%); on.error(Key="Cancelled", Recovery=[goal.call(Name="Caught")])
- assert.equals(Expected="Cancelled", Actual=%caught%, Message="the cancelled task never went on")

Slow
- timer.sleep(Duration="2s")
- goal.return(Data="went on")

Caught
- variable.set(Name=%caught%, Value=%!error.Key%)
